# Shell scripts MUST stay LF, whatever the checkout platform does.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on this machine rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, and a CRLF shell
# script fails on a Linux host in a way that reads like the wrong shell rather than the wrong
# file: bash parses line 2 of `_pod_setup.sh` as `set -euo pipefail\r` and reports
# "pipefail: invalid option name". That cost a pod cycle on 2026-08-10. The round driver also
# normalises scripts on upload, but that only protects the pods -- anyone running these
# directly from a checkout needs the file itself to be right.
*.sh text eol=lf
